WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.525
The most informative comparison in the paper is
turning the semantic map on and off for trajectory prediction.

00:00:04.605 --> 00:00:09.131
For Y-Net,

00:00:09.211 --> 00:00:13.736
adding the map lowers the ADE-twenty from about
0.84 down to 0.68 and the FDE-twenty from about 1.88 to 1.55.

00:00:13.816 --> 00:00:18.342
For NSP-SFM,

00:00:18.422 --> 00:00:22.947
the map brings ADE-twenty from about 0.63 to 0.52
and FDE-twenty from about 1.09 to 0.93.

00:00:23.027 --> 00:00:27.553
In both cases the map helps,

00:00:27.633 --> 00:00:32.158
confirming the value of the scene context that SiT
provides.

00:00:32.238 --> 00:00:36.764
On the detection side,

00:00:36.844 --> 00:00:41.369
models that fuse camera and LiDAR outperform
single-sensor models,

00:00:41.449 --> 00:00:45.975
and voxel-based backbones outperform pillar-based ones,

00:00:46.055 --> 00:00:50.580
with TransFusion using a voxel backbone giving the
best detection score.
